1
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,900
OK.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,300
If you want to adopt an animal,

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:09,700
first we need to know some references.

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:11,400
References?

5
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,400
People we know?

6
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,700
Friends, teachers....

7
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,000
We need to talk to some people about you.

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,300
We want to be sure that you're responsible

9
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:23,100
and that you can take good care of an animal.

10
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,200
Then you have to fill out this form

11
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,600
about your family background.

12
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:28,900
Is that it?

13
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:31,300
No, there's more.

14
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,400
We need to know about your history with animals.

15
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,100
Have you ever owned an animal?

16
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,000
Yes.

17
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,100
We had a cat when I was eight years old.

18
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,500
I love cats.

19
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,600
Do you have any animals now?

20
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,900
Unfortunately, no.

21
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:47,500
Anything else?

22
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,000
We also like to know

23
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
your reasons for wanting an animal.

24
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,300
Just to hold it and cuddle with it.

25
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,700
Just to have as a pet.

26
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:58,500
I love animals.

27
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,600
To have a friend -- a pal.

28
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:05,200
You know, man's best friend is his dog.

29
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,400
And one thing more.

30
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,500
If you're under twenty-one years of age ...

31
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,200
That's me.

32
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,900
Then an adult must sign for you.

33
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:12,500
Uh-oh.

34
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:13,800
No problem.

35
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,100
My parents will think it's a good idea.

36
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:17,300
I'll be back with them.

37
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:20,800
If the real owners don't come to claim Gemma ...

38
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,500
After forty-eight hours.

39
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:24,800
But please call first.

40
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:28,200
Thanks for your information and for being so helpful.

41
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,500
It's my pleasure.

42
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,100
Nice talking to both of you.

43
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:31,900
Thanks again.

44
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:34,700
Bye.

45
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:37,600
Maybe the real owners will come to claim her.

46
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:39,300
Her eyes look so sad.

47
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,000
She must really miss them.

48
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,800
I see you're both animal lovers.

49
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,000
We are.

50
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,140
Good-bye, Miss Aborn.

51
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:46,600
We'll call in a couple of days.

52
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,800
Good-bye, and thanks for bringing Gemma in.

53
00:01:49,800 --> 00:02:00,600
Bye.

54
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:03,000
I keep thinking about the dog -- about Gemma,

55
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,290
alone in the animal shelter.

56
00:02:05,290 --> 00:02:07,300
I know.

57
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:08,790
But I promise you, Alexandra,

58
00:02:08,790 --> 00:02:10,500
the dog is just fine.

59
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:12,800
They're very kind to the animals.

60
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:13,560
I know they are.

61
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:16,400
I mean about her being alone.

62
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:18,100
Even if they are kind to Gemma,

63
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:20,800
she's still alone, without her family.

64
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:22,200
Ready, folks?

65
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,500
Are you ready, Alexandra?

66
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:25,100
Yes, I'm ready.

67
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:28,100
I'll have the chef's salad, please.

68
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:31,400
I will have a cheeseburger, medium rare,

69
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,500
with raw onion, and french fries, please.

70
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:35,700
Anything to drink?

71
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:38,000
A diet cola, please.

72
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,200
Ginger ale with lots of ice for me, thank you.

73
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,000
I've got it.

74
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,400
Thanks.

75
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:44,600
Aren't you surprised

76
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:46,600
that the animal shelter is so careful

77
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:48,200
about finding homes for the animals?

78
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:50,400
No, I'm not.

79
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,200
And a cheeseburger, medium rare,

80
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:54,200
with onion and french fries.

81
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:57,500
And a ginger ale with lots of ice.

82
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:00,100
Salad dressing?

83
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:02,900
Hey, I wanted you to hear my new sound system

84
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:05,200
when the dog scratched on the front door.

85
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,090
Let's finish eating,

86
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:08,400
and then we'll go back to my house.

87
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:10,500
I want you to hear my new tapes.

88
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:32,500
I've got some great new dance music.

89
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:32,700
Hello.

90
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,400
Stewart residence.

91
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:34,800
Hello.

92
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,200
Is Robbie Stewart there?

93
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:36,500
This is he.

94
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:37,700
Who's this?

95
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:40,700
This is Linda Aborn from the animal shelter.

96
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:43,700
It's Linda from the animal shelter.

97
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:44,100
Yes, Linda.

98
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:45,800
Hi.

99
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,600
We have good news and bad news, Robbie.

100
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,800
Oh?

101
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,000
The good news is that the Levinsons have come by

102
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,500
to pick up the dog.

103
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:56,400
The bad news is, you won't be able to adopt the dog.

104
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,000
That's OK.

105
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,900
Come by one day and look at some of the other dogs.

106
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:02,800
I'm sure there's one for you.

107
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,700
Thanks, Robbie.

108
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:07,200
And the Levinsons thank you for bringing their dog to us.

109
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:08,600
Thanks, Linda.

110
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:17,700
Bye.

111
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:19,800
The owners claimed Gemma?

112
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,400
That's right.

113
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:23,800
I'm glad for the dog.

114
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:26,000
I guess I am, too.

115
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,200
She said if I come by,

116
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:31,800
she'll help me find another dog.

117
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:34,800
Come on. Let's dance.
